From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 15:12:54 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] nir: compare only the coordinate components an image uses

nir_lower_robust_access compared the whole four-component coordinate an
image intrinsic carries against a size vector of the dimension's own
width. The padding beyond the dimension is undefined, so an undefined
component could decide the bounds test, and an optimiser that folds the
comparisons together carries the undefined value into the survivor.

Trim the coordinate to the components the dimension uses.
---
 src/compiler/nir/nir_lower_robust_access.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/compiler/nir/nir_lower_robust_access.c b/src/compiler/nir/nir_lower_robust_access.c
index 63dae22e3412341b7adb47f8b0f538eb2471e92c..0a229664016f5a66190a33ddf24aeb561658ad9d 100644
--- a/src/compiler/nir/nir_lower_robust_access.c
+++ b/src/compiler/nir/nir_lower_robust_access.c
@@ -202,7 +202,12 @@ lower_image(nir_builder *b, nir_intrinsic_instr *instr,
    enum glsl_sampler_dim dim = nir_intrinsic_image_dim(instr);
    uint32_t num_coords = nir_image_intrinsic_coord_components(instr);
    bool is_array = nir_intrinsic_image_array(instr);
-   nir_def *coord = instr->src[1].ssa;
+   /* An image intrinsic's coordinate is padded out to four components, and the
+    * padding is undefined. Only the components the dimension actually uses may
+    * reach the bounds comparison, or an undefined component decides it.
+    */
+   nir_def *coord =
+      nir_trim_vector(b, instr->src[1].ssa, num_coords);
 
    /* Get image size. imageSize for cubes returns the size of a single face. */
    unsigned size_components = num_coords;
